# GCOS Personalization — Claude Code development task pack

**Status:** Ready-to-develop task prompts for the **explicitly finalized** Application BFF and FastAPI Direct Sync API scope only. The design is finalized for the items below; this pack **does not claim that the code is already implemented**.

**Architecture baseline:** Latest user-supplied architecture image (November 2026) plus the `GCOS_Diagrams.zip` HLD/LLD/sequence diagrams. Use the files in `Architecture_References/` to understand dependencies. If the repository contradicts the diagrams, describe the conflict instead of silently adopting an old pattern.

## How to use
1. Put this whole folder alongside the Node.js and Python repositories, or supply Claude Code with the target task Markdown file plus `01_FROZEN_ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md` and `02_SHARED_CONTRACTS.md`.
2. Start Claude Code **inside the appropriate repository**. Give it **one** task file at a time, e.g., `Node_BFF/NJS-01_Verify_Google_ID_Token.md`.
3. Ask Claude Code to inspect existing code, implement the scoped change, run tests, and report actual edits. Do not run every task concurrently against the same files.
4. Use the dependency order in `03_IMPLEMENTATION_ORDER.md`. All other architecture work is out of scope pending separate approval (see `04_PENDING_SENIOR_APPROVAL.md`).

